                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I wish I could give this a flat s0-s0 rating. It's not bad for a little while, but it gets stale quickly. It's basically doing the same thing over and over. I mean firefighters do a lot more than just put out fires and drag people out of buildings. That is 95% of what you'll do in this game. I think I had exactly 2 missions that called for the circular saw after playing for over 15 hrs. The AI firemen are dumb as rocks. Sometimes you'll run into a burning house just to find one of the AI firefighters staring at an inferno, holding a hose with no water coming out. The driving is also really horrible. The fire engines turn like some kind of weird tilt-a-whirl. Imagine the way a weathervane rotates. That's exactly the way these engines turn. The fires are almost always way far away from your starting point. This would never happen in real life. Usually there are so many firehouses to cover different neighborhoods. Not in this game. This is like driving from HQ to a fire 3 counties away. Could be a really good game more variety were added to it.",
